    "slug": "showdrop",
    "title": "Showdrop — Ticket Booking Platform",
    "category": "personal",
    "tagline": "BookMyShow-style booking with live seat maps, 5-minute holds and an AI booking assistant.",
    "description": "Browse movies, stand-up and theatre, pick seats on a live map and hold them while you pay. A Spring Boot API guards every seat with Redis locks and optimistic versioning, Kafka fans out confirmations, and a Python agent answers questions and holds seats from chat.",
    "highlights": [
      "Seat holds with Redis SET NX and a 5-minute TTL, plus @Version optimistic locking so two people can never book one seat.",
      "Kafka publishes booking.confirmed to a separate notifications service; scheduled jobs release expired holds.",
      "AI assistant (FastAPI) with RAG over Qdrant and tool calls into the booking API. It can hold seats, but only the user can pay.",
      "React + TypeScript + Redux-Saga frontend behind Nginx; runs as 8 containers in Docker Compose or on a local Kubernetes (kind) cluster."
    ],
